      "role": "user",
      "content": "ok i checked the execution role and it definitely has that policy attached. i also checked the bucket policy and it doesnt have any explicit denies. i'm wondering if maybe there's something about the resource ARN or the way the lambda interacts with the bucket specifically? could it be an issue with the bucket itself or the permissions on the bucket level versus the object level?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The issue might be with the way the Lambda function is interacting with your bucket. AWS Lambda KMS-managed keys have limited permissions to delete objects, but can instead only delete objects if the KMS key remains active. In your case, if you're attaching the IAM role with the policy to a KMS key, it might be preventing the Lambda function from deleting or updating existing objects. This could be something to investigate.",
